# Google Stitch

This app is a React Native Android download manager (Material Design 3). Use **Google Stitch MCP** plus **stitch-skills** for UI design and screen implementation.

Official Stitch: https://stitch.withgoogle.com
Skills source: https://github.com/google-labs-code/stitch-skills

## Before designing or implementing UI

1. Confirm the **stitch** MCP server is available. Discover the tool prefix (often `stitch:`) before calling Stitch tools.
2. Read the matching skill under `.agents/skills/` (Cursor also loads these automatically).
3. Follow `docs/` (PRD, engineering standards, architecture). Stitch output must not contradict those documents.

## Which skill to use

| Intent | Skill |
|---|---|
| Vague UI idea → strong Stitch prompt | `enhance-prompt` |
| New screens from text or images | `stitch-generate-design` |
| Design system in Stitch | `stitch-manage-design-system` |
| Semantic DESIGN.md / anti-generic UI | `taste-design` or `design-md` |
| Convert Stitch screens → React Native | `stitch-react-native` |
| Multi-screen iterative build | `stitch-loop` |
| Upload local HTML/assets to Stitch | `stitch-upload-to-stitch` |
| Existing UI → Stitch | `stitch-code-to-design` |

Prefer **`stitch-react-native`** over `stitch-react-components`, `shadcn-ui`, and `react-vite-dashboard`. This product is React Native, not web.

## Implementation rules

- Keep generated UI on Material Design 3, TypeScript, and existing feature-module patterns.
- Store Stitch artifacts under `.stitch/` (`metadata.json`, `designs/`). Do not skip MCP fetch/audit steps in the React Native skill.
- If Stitch MCP is unauthenticated, tell the user to add `STITCH_API_KEY` in `.cursor/stitch.env` (from https://stitch.withgoogle.com Settings) or run `stitch-mcp init --client cursor --local`, then reload MCP. Do not invent screens from memory.
